  "description": "A caller-driven hashed timing wheel for .NET, allocation-free once warm: O(1) cancel and amortized O(1) schedule, generation-checked timer ids (a stale id never cancels someone else's timer), an occupancy bitmap so a large time jump (backtests, simulations) skips the empty spokes instead of costing O(ticks), and bounded polls that delay due timers rather than drop them. Driven by your own clock: time is a long. Not thread-safe: use it from one thread.",
